get_free_ffmpeg_source_files.py selects ffmpeg source blocks with a regex that
only recognises condition terms wrapped in their own parentheses. Wrapping
use_linux_config lets the parser match the main Linux/x64 block; without it only
~47 of ~259 sources are collected and the resulting ffmpeg build is incomplete.
The parentheses are a no-op for GN itself, so only use_linux_config needs one --
the other terms in the condition do not.

--- third_party/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_generated.gni
+++ third_party/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_generated.gni
@@ -85 +85 @@
-    use_linux_config) {
+    (use_linux_config)) {
